# The F/P's fourth job node, and the last of them. A lash poisons two enemies,
# and what the poison does is explode: every two seconds, five lines, harder
# each time than the last.
#
# The accumulation is the skill. GMS's poison builds on anything that survives
# an explosion, and every helping is worth 60 percentage points of the next
# one, five deep -- so a boss walks 330% to 630% over six explosions and stays
# there. That is what `skill_pct_per_repeat` was built for: the count of
# helpings and the count of explosions are the same number seen from either
# side, because a boss survives all of them.
#
# The two caps decide the damage, not the clock. GMS allows nine explosions on
# one enemy and seventeen across every enemy, and the poison lasts up to twenty
# seconds -- so the count runs out first and the interval only says how the
# nine are spread. Nine at two seconds fill eighteen of the twenty.
#
# GMS publishes no interval: the client, the wiki and namu all say only
# "periodically", and the one number its common block never spends is the three
# crystals a map can hold, not a beat. Two seconds is ours, and it is bounded
# rather than picked -- above 20/9 of a second the nine-explosion cap would be
# dead on a boss, which is the one place GMS wrote it for.
#
# The extra explosion GMS goes out on -- "all poison is removed, followed by an
# additional explosion" -- is not a tick. It lands with the ninth, at the top
# of the ramp, which is `final_repeat_strike`.
#
# The crystal is dropped, and the spread with it. Both are how GMS moves the
# poison off a mob that died, and the total is capped either way: two enemies
# exploding nine times each is eighteen against GMS's seventeen. What is lost
# is that a freshly infected mob starts its ramp again, so a crowd is worth
# somewhat more here than in GMS. A boss, where this skill is measured, has
# nothing to spread to at all.
#
# This poison is NOT a burn. GMS says it plainly -- it does not activate
# Elemental Drain -- so it is a pulse rather than a `dot`, and DoT Punisher's
# orb count and Fervent Drain's final damage never see it.
name: "Poison Chain"
description:
  "Unleash a fatal poison on a chain of enemies. Poisoned enemies "
  "periodically release clouds of additional poison, damaging both "
  "themselves and other nearby enemies. Even if they survive the initial "
  "explosion, the poison effect stacks, raising the power of further "
  "explosions. Unaffected by attack reflection."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 4 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_STAFF
base_delay_ms: 660
cooldown_seconds: 25.0
max_enemies: 2
lines: 4
base { skill_pct: 2.60 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.10 }
buff {
  duration_seconds: 20.0
  pulse {
    label: "Poison Explosion"
    cast_interval_seconds: 2.0
    lines: 5
    max_pulses: 9
    final_repeat_strike: true
    max_repeats: 5
    skill_pct_per_repeat: 0.31
    skill_pct_per_repeat_per_level: 0.01
    base { skill_pct: 1.56 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.06 }
  }
}
